      "content_sha256": "b19f6092dff6e4de1e2284fe604928617d155db07649c5190631b3b22d5c950c",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "expresses a feeling that, although not serious at the moment, there seems to be a sign of or a tendency toward a particular condition, as in, feeling a cold coming on or sensing that one is a little overweight (see my examples above).",
      "html": "expresses a feeling that, although not serious at the moment, there seems to be a sign of or a tendency toward a particular condition, as in, feeling a cold coming on or sensing that one is a little overweight (see my examples above).",
      "credits_raw": "angelitosh2004",
      "content_sha256": "b19295d9d4d685f719f5354d550312828ebca4b27fb6ff8c472773e958d4a594",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "how would you say 'I tend to slack off at work'?\n(is this ok?「仕事やってるときに怠け者気味です」)",
      "html": "how would you say 'I tend to slack off at work'?<br/>(is this ok?「仕事やってるときに怠け者気味です」)",
      "credits_raw": "EvilKyra",
      "content_sha256": "896e4c1d52784fc066d6a69483f70905415983dfa22f69d245afb6de761e7db7",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Yes I am also interested in this question above, it seems right to me.\n\n彼は哀しい気味です。He tends to be a bit sad\n-ish. i know it's not correct English, but people still use \"ish\" to make words. Can it be used in this way with 気味？",
      "html": "Yes I am also interested in this question above, it seems right to me.<br/><br/>彼は哀しい気味です。He tends to be a bit sad<br/>-ish. i know it's not correct English, but people still use \"ish\" to make words. Can it be used in this way with 気味？",
      "credits_raw": "anna.kendall",
      "content_sha256": "cd92892418c371533f6d169f6b76ee5c2229fb8ac5ddc66e2966009586976a41",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "So what is the difference between 「がち」and 「ぎみ」？",
      "html": "So what is the difference between 「がち」and 「ぎみ」？",
      "credits_raw": "erekose200",
      "content_sha256": "a883942fbe2248a92f0307fa7ea0c2592fb5ca1690bcff1b55f81d775997168c",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "The main difference between 「がち」and ぎみ is that 「がち」usually describes a general tendency in someone or something while 「ぎみ」describes a visible indication of a tendency. \ne.g. 1 田中は最近太りがちだ\nTanaka has a general tendency to gain weigh but is not necessarily overweight at the moment of speech。Compare with;\n２）田中は最近太り気味だ\nTanaka is showing signs of being overweight。\n\nAlso 「がち」Cannot express the idea of \"a touch of\" or \" a little\".\n(taken from the Intermediate grammar dictionary)",
      "html": "The main difference between 「がち」and ぎみ is that 「がち」usually describes a general tendency in someone or something while 「ぎみ」describes a visible indication of a tendency. <br/>e.g. 1 田中は最近太りがちだ<br/>Tanaka has a general tendency to gain weigh but is not necessarily overweight at the moment of speech。Compare with;<br/>２）田中は最近太り気味だ<br/>Tanaka is showing signs of being overweight。<br/><br/>Also 「がち」Cannot express the idea of \"a touch of\" or \" a little\".<br/>(taken from the Intermediate grammar dictionary)",
      "credits_raw": "bluntcrayon",
      "content_sha256": "cf28982c73a8aeb3513da438546367d73f817963099ffa3c8cf3082270e4ca85",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "does gimi work with adjectives?\n\nlike 暑い気味",
      "html": "does gimi work with adjectives?<br/><br/>like 暑い気味",
      "credits_raw": "hungry-sumo",
      "content_sha256": "97047fdc21362be8351e736f7f2efbf30f73bd03cc1fa492d3827113b092c668",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "gimi cannot be used with i-adjectives",
